    {
      "caption": "Misconception: a catalyst shifts equilibrium",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s6",
      "narration": "A catalyst is not a shortcut to more product. It lowers the activation energy equally for the forward and reverse reactions, so both speed up by the same factor — the position of equilibrium is unchanged, and Kc is untouched.",
